      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Joseph Sinnott Mansion, listed on the National Register in 1980, now serves as part of The Mansion at Rosemont senior‑living community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rosemont straddles the Philadelphia Main Line, lying partly in Lower Merion Township and partly in Radnor Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Both the Paoli/Thorndale Line and the Norristown High Speed Line stop in Rosemont, making it a key rail hub on the Main Line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Agnes Irwin School, an all‑girl day school founded by Miss Agnes Irwin, occupies Ithan Avenue and has educated generations in Rosemont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 1894 Gothic‑revival Church of the Good Shepherd anchors Rosemont’s religious heritage and remains a landmark of the community.",
